{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `y_safestan_flat`, a deterministic row-major flattening of the original response array `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: added `y_safestan_flat` with deterministic relation `y_safestan_flat[(i - 1) * J + j] = y[i, j]` for Stan indices `i = 1:I` and `j = 1:J`. This is needed because the original model scored indexed slices `y[i]` inside a loop, while SafeStan requires the protected observation to be a top-level identifier scored exactly once. The likelihood was rewritten as one vectorized `bernoulli_logit` statement over the flattened responses, with linear predictors computed in the same row-major order. The parameter priors were already explicit and are unchanged.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=1> I; // // items
  int<lower=1> J; // // students
  array[I, J] int<lower=0, upper=1> y; // boolean correctness of student j on item i for n
  array[I * J] int<lower=0, upper=1> y_safestan_flat;
}
parameters {
  vector[J] alpha; // ability for student j
  vector[I] beta; // difficulty for item i
  vector<lower=0>[I] delta; // discriminativeness for item i
}
model {
  vector[I * J] eta;

  alpha ~ normal(0, 1);
  beta ~ normal(0, 5);
  delta ~ gamma(2, 2);

  for (i in 1 : I) {
    for (j in 1 : J) {
      eta[(i - 1) * J + j] = delta[i] * (alpha[j] - beta[i]);
    }
  }

  y_safestan_flat ~ bernoulli_logit(eta);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"I":3,"J":1,"y":[[0],[0],[0]],"y_safestan_flat":[0,0,0]}","protected_variables":["y_safestan_flat"]}
